 ## 0. Release policy slot — USER SELECTION REQUIRED
 
 ```text
-RELEASE_POLICY = UNSET        allowed values: P-HARD | P-ACCEPT
+RELEASE_POLICY = P-ACCEPT     allowed values: P-HARD | P-ACCEPT
 ```
+
+**Selection note (2026-10-14).** The user selected P-ACCEPT. The evidence is `round17-paid-comparison/run/CAP-ACCEPTANCE.json` (sha256 `c0dfc30914b96fe369f2124f4f7aca88a4c0e5786c7892767995cab8ae40fa06`) and `round17-paid-comparison/run/KEY-ATTESTATION.json` (sha256 `f6f3eae8813a390a1133f55b9b990ae537c68a90b09e3e8d7dc619bdf547b338`). This release reads the frozen design together with four amendments: A1, P5 fixture gate in batches (`round17-paid-comparison/amendments/A1-p5-batching/AMENDMENT.md`, `b683f32129a0fed549941fd492e31cc5aa701a16ecb88e3d3cc46bd5a61734fe`); A2, packet file delivery (`round17-paid-comparison/amendments/A2-packet-file-delivery/AMENDMENT.md`, `3827175eb37c0e4b473923f79fa5cdce4ff1152122d9427ce9bb9f2d5667aa7e`); A3, a 600 s POST response timeout (`round17-paid-comparison/release-prep/A3-TIMEOUT.md`, `3a9c7c3a626dd9776013a3942891556bbfdcde8eab807f081d29bd3a29eee091`); and A4, `KEY_MAX` $50.00 and key label `DocketClock` (`round17-paid-comparison/amendments/A4-key-limit-label/AMENDMENT.md`, `d8826cf2b8f6ec5add43aa027af9cb8529ea21b69a2e90b2b13e13631d1c3538`). Under A4, the $1.73 key limit in this section and in §1 and §4 is superseded. The provider key limit caps spend at $50.00, and the $2.00 bound rests on the ledger (§4) and CN1–CN4. All other text in this file is unchanged from `../design-r3-1/`.
 
 The user replaces `UNSET` with exactly one value here and in `READY.json` (`release_policy`). The same value is written into `INIT` and the release record, and admission refuses `UNSET`, a missing or unknown value, or any disagreement between `INIT` and `BIND_RELEASE` (§4 rule 4; L19–L23). That check is defense in depth. Whether the policy's evidence (E-1/E-2 acceptance, or the user's written acceptance) exists and is accepted is a recorded human decision that the release gate (PROTOCOL P7) verifies; selecting a value alone never satisfies it. Nothing else in this design changes with the choice: every mechanism in §1–§5 applies under both variants, and each variant below is complete as written. **While the value is `UNSET`, the paid phase stays unreleased.** An approval of a hard cap is not an acceptance of a conditional budget, and this design does not infer one.
 
